          ],
          "prerequisites": [],
          "lessons": [
            {
              "id": "b1-grammar-infinitive-constructions-lesson-1",
              "topicId": "b1-grammar-infinitive-constructions",
              "categoryId": "b1-grammar",
              "levelId": "b1",
              "title": "anfangen + zu + Infinitiv (Natural German)",
              "shortDescription": "Understand why Ich fange an, Deutsch zu lernen is natural and Ich fange Deutsch zu lernen an sounds heavy.",
              "order": 1,
              "estimatedMinutes": 35,
              "sections": [
                {
                  "type": "explanation",
                  "title": "1) سوال رایج زبان آموزان",
                  "content": "English:\nMany learners ask: Why is an in the middle in Ich fange an, Deutsch zu lernen?\n\nفارسی:\nخیلی از زبان آموزان می پرسند چرا در جمله Ich fange an, Deutsch zu lernen بخش an در میانه جمله می آید و نه آخر جمله."
                },
                {
                  "type": "warning",
                  "title": "2) Natural vs unnatural phrasing",
                  "content": "Less natural (understandable but heavy): Und warum fangen Sie Deutsch zu lernen an?\nNatural and standard: Und warum fangen Sie an, Deutsch zu lernen?\n\nEnglish:\nThe first sentence is not strictly ungrammatical, but it sounds old, heavy, and non-native in modern usage.\n\nفارسی:\nجمله اول از نظر درک معنایی ممکن است قابل فهم باشد، اما در آلمانی طبیعی امروز سنگین و غیرطبیعی به گوش می رسد."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "title": "3) Core pattern comparison",
                  "headers": [
                    "Case",
                    "Formula",
                    "Example"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    ["Conjugated separable verb", "Subject + verb stem + ... + prefix", "Er fangt morgen an."],
                    ["Separable infinitive with zu", "prefix + zu + verb", "anzufangen"],
                    ["Conjugated verb + infinitive group", "Subject + verb stem + prefix, + infinitive group", "Ich fange an, Deutsch zu lernen."]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "tip",
                  "title": "4) The key B1 rule",
                  "content": "If the separable verb itself appears as a zu-infinitive, use one word: anfangen -> anzufangen, aufstehen -> aufzustehen, einkaufen -> einzukaufen. But if the separable verb is conjugated, keep normal split and then attach the infinitive group after a comma."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "title": "5) Mini-grid: Why an is before the comma",
                  "headers": [
                    "Part",
                    "Function",
                    "In sentence"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    ["Ich", "Subject", "Ich"],
                    ["fange", "Finite verb stem", "fange"],
                    ["an", "Separable prefix", "an"],
                    ["Deutsch zu lernen", "Infinitive group", "Deutsch zu lernen"]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "title": "6) Correct model sentence",
                  "content": "DE: Und warum fangen Sie an, Deutsch zu lernen?\nEN: And why are you starting to learn German?\nFA: و چرا شروع می کنید آلمانی یاد بگیرید؟"
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "title": "7) Three high-frequency examples",
                  "headers": [
                    "German",
                    "English",
                    "فارسی"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    ["Ich versuche, fruh aufzustehen.", "I try to get up early.", "من تلاش می کنم زود بیدار شوم."],
                    ["Er versucht, morgen anzufangen.", "He tries to start tomorrow.", "او تلاش می کند فردا شروع کند."],
                    ["Ich fange an, mit meinem Bruder Deutsch zu lernen.", "I start learning German with my brother.", "من شروع می کنم با برادرم آلمانی یاد بگیرم."]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "title": "8) جمع بندی خیلی مهم",
                  "items": [
                    "Conjugated separable verb: fangt ... an",
                    "Separable zu-infinitive: anzufangen",
                    "Natural modern pattern with infinitive group: Ich fange an, Deutsch zu lernen.",
                    "The A2 to B1 jump is exactly this distinction."
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "vocabulary": [
                {
                  "german": "die Infinitivgruppe",
                  "english": "infinitive group",
                  "persian": "گروه مصدری",
                  "example": "Deutsch zu lernen ist eine Infinitivgruppe."
                },
                {
                  "german": "natürlich",
                  "english": "natural (native-like)",
                  "persian": "طبیعی",
                  "example": "Diese Variante klingt natürlich."
                },
                {
                  "german": "schwerfällig",
                  "english": "heavy, clunky",
                  "persian": "سنگین و نچسب",
                  "example": "Dieser Satz klingt schwerflällig."
                }
              ],
              "exercises": []
            }
          ]
        },
